  "wireForm": "`descriptorBytes` (`ext.json`) and `manifestBytes` (`manifest.json` in the image) are exact bytes: JSON with no whitespace and every object's keys in sorted order, which a reader re-serializes and compares. The descriptor is not signed; `extId` is the SHA-256 of its bytes, and a reader accepts it only when the manifest in the signed image agrees with it on name, version, arch and kernel, and the kernel it is to run on is `kernel` (id, release and arch)"
